    {
      "id": 242586,
      "name": "doppelgangerung",
      "username": "doppelgangerung",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/doppelgangerung/{size}/1876_2.png",
      "created_at": "2022-02-10T15:12:20.020Z",
      "cooked": "<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/8/8252c5ccb64ebf3b177ab98b9b53972ed2b19665.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/8252c5ccb64ebf3b177ab98b9b53972ed2b19665\" title=\"Screenshot_20220208-104623\"><img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/8/8252c5ccb64ebf3b177ab98b9b53972ed2b19665_2_219x500.jpeg\" alt=\"Screenshot_20220208-104623\" data-base62-sha1=\"iATpsW5Mi1Z1dXTqi4ZMiwG3oRD\" width=\"219\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/8/8252c5ccb64ebf3b177ab98b9b53972ed2b19665_2_219x500.jpeg, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/8/8252c5ccb64ebf3b177ab98b9b53972ed2b19665_2_328x750.jpeg 1.5x, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/8/8252c5ccb64ebf3b177ab98b9b53972ed2b19665_2_438x1000.jpeg 2x\" data-small-upload=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/8/8252c5ccb64ebf3b177ab98b9b53972ed2b19665_2_10x10.png\"><div class=\"meta\">\n<svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">Screenshot_20220208-104623</span><span class=\"informations\">1080×2460 163 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg>\n</div></a></div><br>\nPretty straightforward mint - Tech Singularity luckily came out before the team had much equipment in play, many drones got shredded, and even Electro Pulse Explosive could only sit around looking scary with three Hypersonic Assaults in Tachyon’s hand.<br>\nCourtesy of Ra, the heroes were immune to fire damage for most of the game, blunting many of the environment’s dangers, but limiting the Sun God’s options. Haka pounded on things with great gusto, and Visionary mostly rooted around in everyone’s hands trying to get them set up for victory.<br>\nMy storybook ending would have been a Wrest The Mind on one of the EPEs, with Visionary protected by her Cocoon or Ra’s Flesh Of The Sun God/Imbued Fire - but ran out of ways to stall before i got the cards to pull it off, and had to settle for redirecting all that lovely damage back on its source(s) with a WtM and Tachyon’s Synaptic Interruption. T did finally draw a Lightspeed Barrage to finish off Omnitron himself, and Ra slagged the last device with a Fire Blast.</p>",
